WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.020
- So Brooke, you created a platform

00:00:02.020 --> 00:00:04.250
for women over 40 starting a new chapters,

00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:06.000
which I think is fantastic.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.710
- It is called Beginning Is Now,

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:11.440
and I really just, especially
during Covid, I thought,

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:16.440
I'm 56 right but I feel
stronger, I feel more powerful,

00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:19.360
I feel more confident, I don't feel as-

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:20.980
- I feel like that happens with age.

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:21.870
- [Brooke] And that's-
- Yeah.

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:23.650
- [Brooke] The part to
me that's so amazing.

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:26.720
But when you're over 40 and
you look at what's out there,

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:28.471
we're not marketed too, I don't know-

00:00:28.471 --> 00:00:30.550
- But there's not like a lot
of like movies or TV shows,

00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:33.090
it's usually like a specific,
like younger or then older.

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:35.270
It's like, there's nothing
generally in that gap-

00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:36.210
- Yeah, it's like 20s

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:38.750
or Helen Mirren and she's gorgeous but-

00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:41.472
- [Kelly] Yeah, oh my God, I hate her.

00:00:41.472 --> 00:00:42.305
Like who looks like that?

00:00:42.305 --> 00:00:43.220
- [Kirsten] I think one of
the things is though too,

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:45.400
I feel like I'm at this
age too as an actress

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:47.790
where I'm like, do I just age nicely?

00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:49.620
Or like, I think I just gotta get old

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:51.980
so that I can keep with
having good parts too.

00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:54.330
Like I kinda have to just like not fall

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:58.370
for the praise of Los Angeles
and just kinda age normally

00:00:58.370 --> 00:00:59.252
so you're doing a-

00:00:59.252 --> 00:01:00.700
- Well you're doing a beautiful job of it.

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:01.640
- I keep working though.

00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:03.450
I feel like to get interesting parts,

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:04.283
you know what I mean?

00:01:04.283 --> 00:01:05.920
- It is, it's a hard thing
and I've talked to a lot of...

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:06.753
And you know what?

00:01:06.753 --> 00:01:08.080
I never had that conversation with actors,

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:09.310
it's always actresses and it's-

00:01:09.310 --> 00:01:10.560
- Oh yeah.

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:11.577
- And it's always 'cause
there's a harder thing

00:01:11.577 --> 00:01:13.000
that's always put on women.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:15.950
- [Kirsten] Like what, yeah,
how it like, what route?

00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:17.040
- [Brooke] Yep, Netflix was really-

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:18.260
- [Kelly] And how natural can I age?

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:20.620
- Well you don't want your,
half your conversation

00:01:20.620 --> 00:01:21.770
about your part,

00:01:21.770 --> 00:01:23.777
like the supporting
conversation to be like,

00:01:23.777 --> 00:01:25.170
"Oh what face work did she do?"

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:26.003
You know what I mean?

00:01:26.003 --> 00:01:27.381
Like, which would be devastating to me.

00:01:27.381 --> 00:01:28.619
- Is that a real-

00:01:28.619 --> 00:01:30.020
- [Brooke] Oh yes.
- [Kirsten] Yeah.

00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:30.950
- Well what Netflix,

00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:34.070
when they originally
talked to me about it,

00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:37.087
it was a woman who in this
one particular division said,

00:01:37.087 --> 00:01:41.090
"We are interested in
women over a certain age."

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:42.120
Over 40, they're saying.

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:44.650
Because there're empowered women in there.

00:01:44.650 --> 00:01:46.950
And she said, "That's what
we're gearing towards."

00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:50.890
So it's really, it's lovely
that to hear a network

00:01:50.890 --> 00:01:52.810
say that that's their focus, you know,

00:01:52.810 --> 00:01:55.720
and it's a section of Netflix, you know,

00:01:55.720 --> 00:01:58.885
but it is, they, and that's
what she wants to do,

00:01:58.885 --> 00:02:03.190
this executive, and I was
so happy that, you know,

00:02:03.190 --> 00:02:06.570
they weren't trying to make me eat 30.

00:02:06.570 --> 00:02:07.403
Do you know what I mean?

00:02:07.403 --> 00:02:11.070
Like it's, I was my age
and I was acting my age

00:02:11.070 --> 00:02:14.970
and in myself, and really
just there's pride in it,

00:02:14.970 --> 00:02:17.500
and I love that there's
starting to be representation

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:19.680
like that in at least in these movies.

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:22.620
- And as a woman that's about
to be 40, I love watching it.

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:24.800
Like, I don't really
relate, sorry, anymore

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:26.600
to a lot of the younger, like,
you know what I'm saying?

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:27.500
There's, there's like,

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:29.120
there should be like
sections for all of it.

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:30.410
Like, we like to watch different things,

00:02:30.410 --> 00:02:32.350
and maybe people, I don't
know our own age doing stuff.

00:02:32.350 --> 00:02:33.620
So yeah.
- And there's romance,

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:36.710
you know, and there's humor
and there's, you know, it's,

00:02:36.710 --> 00:02:39.580
there's, it's parts of it that
are sort of just sexy enough,

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:40.520
you know what I mean?

00:02:40.520 --> 00:02:42.260
But, but it's, and it's presenting women

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:44.340
with all of their facets, you know?

00:02:44.340 --> 00:02:45.860
And I think that that's...

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:49.590
It took me decades to grow into myself

00:02:49.590 --> 00:02:52.137
and not compare myself or say,

00:02:52.137 --> 00:02:53.630
"Oh God, they want me to do this,

00:02:53.630 --> 00:02:55.440
or I'm not this enough
or I'm not that another."

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:56.330
- Well the reason why you
probably did that though

00:02:56.330 --> 00:02:57.740
is 'cause people put that
on us when we're young.

00:02:57.740 --> 00:03:00.060
- [Kirsten] They do, especially,
yeah, are you kidding me?

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:01.840
Of course, yeah, all of us

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:03.860
like had different versions of that.

00:03:03.860 --> 00:03:05.750
You probably had it the
worst, Brooke, right?

00:03:05.750 --> 00:03:08.380
I mean-
- I mean, I wasn't, I mean,

00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:09.950
there was no social media when I was-

00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:11.050
- That's true.
- You know?

00:03:11.050 --> 00:03:12.080
I mean, it was...

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:15.320
I had my own set of different things

00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:17.020
that I had to grapple
with, insecurity wise,

00:03:17.020 --> 00:03:18.400
but it was, you know,

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:20.630
I was called a face of
a decade, it's like-

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:21.670
- And that's a lot of pressure.

00:03:21.670 --> 00:03:23.220
- Who decides that, you know?
- It's a lot of pressure-

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:26.480
- Feel free to call mine
the face of the decade.

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:29.942
I don't know who decides, but
no, that's a lot of pressure-

00:03:29.942 --> 00:03:31.980
- The arbitrary ridiculousness of it.

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:35.880
So what I did was became the
class clown, self-deprecate.

00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:37.263
- Oh me too.
- Oh look at me, look at me,

00:03:37.263 --> 00:03:38.790
waka, waka, waka.

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:41.830
And I need to diffuse
the air, I need to have,

00:03:41.830 --> 00:03:43.930
not be threatening to women, I need to-

00:03:43.930 --> 00:03:47.070
- Oh my God, that's how I
feel sometimes too, yeah.

00:03:47.070 --> 00:03:48.870
- And then you start to believe it,

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:52.730
then you start living in
your comments about yourself

00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:54.820
and your self-deprecation and you know,

00:03:54.820 --> 00:03:56.360
and that's not healthy either.

00:03:56.360 --> 00:04:00.010
And so it's about finding
that balance of saying,

00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:03.870
you know, I mean, by
virtue of getting older,

00:04:03.870 --> 00:04:05.850
I would be considered a disappointment

00:04:05.850 --> 00:04:09.200
because I would've had to have
died when I was, you know,

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:11.180
18 or something like
that to, it's not funny,

00:04:11.180 --> 00:04:13.630
but like to preserve

00:04:13.630 --> 00:04:16.780
what everybody has on their
psyche about me, right?

00:04:16.780 --> 00:04:17.613
- Because at the end of the day,

00:04:17.613 --> 00:04:18.780
sometimes people view you as a product

00:04:18.780 --> 00:04:20.960
and not the actual person,
so they just see one thing,

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:22.590
yeah, totally.
- And so I had to,

00:04:22.590 --> 00:04:26.770
throughout my life really
just reveal myself emotionally

00:04:26.770 --> 00:04:30.570
and in all ways so that that's
what I could own, you know?

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:32.100
So it wasn't just-
- I feel the same,

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:34.200
like same in a different way too, yeah.

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:36.110
Yeah, I was lucky working
with Sofia Coppola

00:04:36.110 --> 00:04:38.470
at such a young age, because at 16,

00:04:38.470 --> 00:04:40.030
when you don't feel good about yourself,

00:04:40.030 --> 00:04:41.300
she made me feel beautiful.

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:44.590
So I had that to kind of
take me through the like

00:04:44.590 --> 00:04:48.850
more masculine, like,
energy films and things.

00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:51.490
I didn't look to anybody
or dress in a certain way

00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:53.700
on the carpet that like I had to be sexy.

00:04:53.700 --> 00:04:55.020
I dressed the way I
wanted to dress, you know?

00:04:55.020 --> 00:04:56.420
- That's a beautiful thing
to have that influence

00:04:56.420 --> 00:04:57.480
so from a woman at a young age.

00:04:57.480 --> 00:05:00.610
- I got lucky that I had that
at such a young age, yeah.

00:05:00.610 --> 00:05:01.830
- [Brooke] And I never had that,

00:05:01.830 --> 00:05:05.238
and I got male directors
who loved the men-

00:05:05.238 --> 00:05:06.690
- We might edit this out.

00:05:06.690 --> 00:05:07.707
I had a photographer literally
look at me, and I was,

00:05:09.770 --> 00:05:11.490
it was literally right
after American Idol,

00:05:11.490 --> 00:05:13.607
and it was like 20 years
ago, and it was, he was like,

00:05:13.607 --> 00:05:16.000
"Man, you would be so pretty
if you lost 20 pounds."

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:16.960
And I was like, "Oh my God,

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:18.410
how much weight do you
think you need to lose

00:05:18.410 --> 00:05:19.420
to be attractive?"

00:05:19.420 --> 00:05:21.474
- Awesome that you said that by the way!

00:05:21.474 --> 00:05:22.531
I love that you said that back to him.

00:05:22.531 --> 00:05:23.481
(audience applauding)

